From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Anze <aanzdev@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 27 Jul 2026 18:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] usb: typec: mux: zero-init the switch match array

fwnode_typec_switch_get() declares the match array on the stack without
initialising it:

	struct typec_switch_dev *sw_devs[TYPEC_MUX_MAX_DEVS];

and passes it to fwnode_connection_find_matches(), which fills the slots
one at a time. The dedup loop in typec_switch_match() reads every slot
before fwnode_connection_find_matches() has filled them, so a valid
switch can be dropped by a chance comparison against stack garbage.

(The -EPROBE_DEFER half of the original patch is already upstream in
7.2; only the zero-initialisation was left.)

Signed-off-by: Anze <aanzdev@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/usb/typec/mux.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/typec/mux.c b/drivers/usb/typec/mux.c
--- a/drivers/usb/typec/mux.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/typec/mux.c
@@ -81,7 +81,7 @@
  */
 struct typec_switch *fwnode_typec_switch_get(struct fwnode_handle *fwnode)
 {
-	struct typec_switch_dev *sw_devs[TYPEC_MUX_MAX_DEVS];
+	struct typec_switch_dev *sw_devs[TYPEC_MUX_MAX_DEVS] = {};
 	struct typec_switch *sw;
 	int count;
 	int err;
